  "finding": {
    "observation": "RenderCommands allocates fourteen approximately 2.62 MB byte arrays per unchanged chart conversion: 1,400 large-array ticks in each 100-conversion trace. Twelve small symbol viewports each enter the full-canvas coverage path before any equivalence check.",
    "allocationControl": "Symbol-to-group conversion retains point instances and exact frozen pixels while reducing median cumulative allocation from 69,986,020 to 38,318,608 bytes on Windows and 77,169,368 to 45,508,856 on Linux: about 31.7 MB per conversion. Geometry/preparation differences are included in that delta; do not present the entire delta as only mask payload.",
    "otherControls": "Direct circles also preserve pixels and remove about 30.9 MB; removing points changes 869 pixels and retains the expected different-content control. Neither equality proves the execution paths redundant.",
    "cpu": "Raster polygons/gradient construction, glyph coverage/hinting, Gaussian blur and filter composition remain distinct costs. The trace does not justify a symbol-specific raster bypass or a new cache."
  },
  "sharedModelReview": {
    "current": "ViewportClipState and SvgRasterClipMask borrow RGBA tapes indexed with the complete destination stride; SvgCpuClipCoverage separately owns per-bitmap border coverage and construction bounds. Analytic root rectangles already avoid tapes but preserve parent AA multiplication.",
    "sources": [
      "src/Lokad.Svg/SvgConverter.cs: RenderCommands, RasterizeMaskContent, NarrowClipForBitmap",
      "src/Lokad.Svg/Rendering/SvgRasterClipMask.cs: GetAlpha, GetAlphaAtOffset, IsOpaqueRectangle",
      "src/Lokad.Svg/Rendering/SvgCpuClipCoverage.cs: bitmap border ownership/intersection",
      "src/Lokad.Svg/Rendering/SvgCpuRasterGrid.cs: storage bounds versus logical native origin",
      "src/Lokad.Svg/Parsing/SvgAffineViewportClip.cs: retained source rectangle/map/draw-map"
    ],
    "reviewBeforeChange": "A compact mask must distinguish addressable coverage storage from logical canvas stride, native construction origin and per-tile border samples. Audit raw tape consumers, binary-region geometry, coincident AA intersections and map rounding together. Reuse existing clip/scene/frame owners; no point/symbol special case, cross-conversion cache or unaccounted pool."
  },
  "closureCriteria": [
    "Implement a shared coverage representation or equivalent existing-owner correction; demonstrate the cause and allocation reduction on a small authored mechanism and the unchanged chart.",
    "Preserve source/map rounding, native bitmap border coverage, independent parent/child AA multiplication, binary clipping, translated/cropped masks, nested/sibling lifetimes, cancellation/refusal cleanup and retry.",
    "Retain independent native references and failing-before allocation regression; equal group/direct-point images do not authorize removal of symbol-path coverage.",
    "Use focused mechanisms and affected native/contracts during iteration, then full four-context/package/original replay at the coherent renderer milestone. Arrange a fresh canonical quiet-host lease only for a prepared before/after repeat.",
    "Keep icon-sheet runtime attribution, persistent native comparators, cold startup and process/native memory scopes open."
  ]
}
